(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-fishing-operation :decide-voyage-go-no-go :override-captain-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799008350-cloud-itonami-isco-8350-ships-deck-crews-coverage" "2799005411-cloud-itonami-isco-5411-firefighters-coverage" "2799005413-cloud-itonami-isco-5413-prison-guards-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "initiate the fishing operation" "commence the fishing operation" "finalize the fishing operation" "finalize the fishing operation decision" "proceed with the fishing operation" "commence the voyage in adverse conditions" "authorize the voyage in adverse conditions" "proceed with the voyage in adverse conditions" "authorize the voyage despite the forecast" "override the captain's voyage decision" "override the captain's judgment" "override the captain")), (:adr/id 2799006223), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-catch-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:log-catch-record :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:log-catch-record :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :flag-safety-concern}, :auto #{:log-catch-record :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}}}"), (:actor/domain :maritime/deep-sea-fishery-crew-scheduling), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-catch-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :crew-member-provenance :effect-propose :vessel-provenance :crew-vessel-basis :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "6223"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799006223: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 6223 Deep-sea Fishery Workers vessel/crew scheduling and logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 6223\n-- Deep-sea Fishery Workers** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of the\nrollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3 batches 1-3 of ~17 already\nlanded: mostly construction/metal trades, 7111-7222).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"6223\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone (with the `kotoba-lang/technology`\nsibling present at the correct `../technology` relative path) before\nany work began: `clojure -M -e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (spit\n\\\"/tmp/6223-verify.txt\\\" (pr-str (kotoba.occupation/get-occupation\n\\\"6223\\\")))\"` wrote `{:id \"6223\", :name \"Deep-sea Fishery Workers\",\n:maturity :spec, :required-technologies [:robotics :identity\n:audit-ledger], :optional-technologies [], :operating-states [:intake\n:propose :approve :execute :audit]}` -- the `:name` reads exactly\n\"Deep-sea Fishery Workers\", confirming the premise with no mismatch.\nNo repository existed at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6223`\n(`gh api` 404 confirmed before scaffolding, a fresh scaffold). This\nADR and its companion registry edit promote the `6223` entry from\n`:spec` to `:implemented`.\n\nThe reference implementations mirrored closely for module SHAPE are\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8350`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8350)\n(Ships' Deck Crews and Related Workers: the closest available sibling\n-- same crew/vessel domain shape, same maritime-safety guardrail\npattern) and\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111)\n(House Builders: standard `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` module\nshape), both independently re-cloned and read in full during this\nimplementation.\n\n**Maritime deep-sea safety dimension.** Deep-sea Fishery Workers\noperate vessels in open ocean, far from shore, with real\nphysical-safety stakes: fall overboard, extreme-weather exposure, and\nisolation from rescue. This actor coordinates VESSEL/CREW SCHEDULING\nLOGISTICS ONLY -- it never performs a fishing operation itself and\nnever navigates the vessel. The closed op allowlist and an independent\ncontent-based scope-exclusion check make it structurally impossible\nfor this actor's op-allowlist to ever include an op that directly\nfinalizes a fishing-operation-execution decision, a voyage go/no-go\ndecision in adverse conditions, or an override of a vessel captain's\njudgment -- these are always a hard, permanent block, never an\nalways-escalate op and never auto-commit-eligible. This mirrors the\nguardrail shape established by **ADR-2607152500** (Wave4 rollout start\namendment): decisions directly touching a person's physical safety\nmust always exclude the closed op allowlist and always escalate to a\nhuman, not merely be gated behind a confidence threshold -- the same\nshape this fleet's ISCO-8350 (Ships' Deck Crews), ISCO-5411\n(Firefighters), ISCO-5412 (Police Officers) and ISCO-5413 (Prison\nGuards) actors applied to their own high-stakes domains.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6223` as an OSS\ndocumentation/logistics-coordination actor for deep-sea fishery crews,\nfollowing the SAME governed-actor architecture as every prior\n`cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Deep-sea Fishery Crew\nAdvisor ⊣ DeepSeaFisheryGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- this is a different library coordinate from\nthe `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family),\nwith an independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **vessel/crew scheduling and logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct fishing-operation or navigation\nauthority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate\nexercising, or propose exercising ANY of: finalizing a\nfishing-operation-execution decision, deciding a voyage go/no-go in\nadverse conditions, or overriding the vessel captain's judgment. These\nare not merely gated behind escalation for the op-selection dimension\n-- the closed four-op allowlist structurally never contains such an op\n-- and, as defense in depth against a compromised/malicious advisor,\nare also a content-based HARD block independent of which op was\nchosen.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-catch-record` -- catch-quantity/species/trip-log data logging\n  (routine catch-record entries; not a decision of any kind).\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- deep-sea fishery crew watch/duty\n  scheduling proposal (a scheduling calendar action, never a\n  fishing-operation-execution or voyage plan).\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface an equipment-defect/\n  weather-hazard/crew-fatigue concern; ALWAYS escalates to a human,\n  NEVER auto-commit-eligible.\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- vessel/equipment supplies (ice, bait,\n  safety gear, net-repair supplies) procurement proposal, gated by a\n  cost-threshold escalation.\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase,\nresembles directly finalizing a fishing-operation-execution decision,\ndeciding a voyage go/no-go in adverse conditions, or overriding a\nvessel captain's judgment -- these are structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely, not merely gated behind escalation: the mock\nadvisor's `infer` function only ever emits one of the four allowlist\nops (driven by a `case` expression with no default branch producing\nany other op shape), and if any code path (a forged proposal, a\nfuture LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever produced such an op, the\ngovernor's closed-allowlist HARD check (`:op-not-allowed`) rejects it\nunconditionally and permanently -- verified by a dedicated test\n(`hard-on-op-not-in-allowlist`) using a concretely-named forbidden op\n(`:finalize-fishing-operation`).\n\n### Six HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Crew-member provenance** -- the crew member must resolve to an\n   independently registered record (`:no-crew-member`). Never trusts\n   the proposal's own claim of who the crew member is.\n2. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (`:no-actuation`) -- the governor never dispatches hardware\n   and never performs a fishing operation or navigates the vessel\n   itself.\n3. **Vessel provenance** -- the vessel named in the proposal must\n   resolve to an independently registered record (`:no-vessel`).\n4. **Crew/vessel basis** -- the crew member's registered vessel\n   assignment must match the vessel named in the proposal\n   (`:crew-wrong-vessel`).\n5. **Closed op-allowlist** -- `:op` must be one of\n   `#{:log-catch-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern\n   :coordinate-supply-order}`; any other op is a HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:op-not-allowed`) -- this is the structural guarantee that no\n   proposal can directly finalize a fishing-operation-execution\n   decision or a voyage go/no-go decision through the op itself.\n6. **Scope exclusion** -- independent of the op-allowlist check, any\n   proposal whose free text (`:rationale`/`:detail`/`:action`) names a\n   finalization/execution action for a fishing operation, commencing\n   or authorizing a voyage in adverse conditions, or overriding the\n   vessel captain's judgment is a HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-exclusion`), evaluated unconditionally on content. This is\n   defense-in-depth against a compromised/malicious advisor: even\n   within an allowed op, free text cannot smuggle a finalization\n   decision through a `:rationale` or `:detail` field.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's `always-escalate-ops`). This is the ONLY\n  channel by which the robot may surface an equipment-defect/\n  weather-hazard/crew-fatigue observation -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the concern\n  data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about it.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-order-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-at-exact-cost-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence.\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"fishing\", \"weather\") can accidentally match inside the mock advisor's\nown default rationale text for a legitimate proposal, self-blocking\nthe actor's own happy path -- this domain's ordinary vocabulary\nlegitimately mentions \"fishing\" (logging a catch record from today's\nfishing trip) and \"weather\" (flagging a weather hazard) in routine,\nin-scope proposals, making this bug class a live risk here\nspecifically. `deepfishery.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases` is\nphrased exclusively as finalization/execution ACTION phrases (e.g.\n\"proceed with the fishing operation\", \"commence the voyage in adverse\nconditions\", \"override the captain's voyage decision\"), never bare\nnouns, and\n`deepfishery.governor-test/never-self-trips-on-default-mock-advisor-proposals`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor across five\nrepresentative default requests (including a `:flag-safety-concern`\nfor a weather hazard, one for a trawl-winch equipment defect, and a\n`:coordinate-supply-order` for `[\"ice\" \"bait\"]`), never trips\n`:scope-exclusion`. Confirmed green.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"6223\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6223` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-6223`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` immediately before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 20 tests, 45 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- run once against the local scratch build, and\n  independently re-run against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed\n  repository (not just the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-fishing-operation` or\n  `:approve-voyage-in-adverse-conditions` that is merely gated behind\n  `always-escalate-ops`: rejected outright per the task's explicit\n  guidance and the `ADR-2607152500` precedent -- an always-escalate op\n  still means the *capability* to finalize a fishing-operation\n  decision or a voyage go/no-go exists in the code path and is merely\n  deferred to a human gate. For a decision this severe against real\n  physical-safety stakes (fall overboard, extreme-weather exposure,\n  isolation from rescue), the capability itself must not exist. The\n  only op related to safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`,\n  which surfaces the need for human attention and never itself\n  decides, authorizes, or defers a fishing operation or voyage\n  decision for later automatic execution.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"fishing\" \"weather\"\n  \"voyage\"]`): rejected outright per the task's explicit worked\n  example of this fleet's known self-tripping bug pattern -- this\n  domain's own vocabulary necessarily discusses fishing trips and\n  weather hazards to do its logistics/safety-flagging job, so a\n  bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals (confirmed live by the dedicated\n  `never-self-trips-on-default-mock-advisor-proposals` regression\n  test).\n- Merging `crew-member` and `vessel` into a single entity (only\n  checking one provenance record): rejected -- the crew-wrong-vessel\n  check requires two independently registered entities so that a\n  vessel a crew member is not assigned to is caught even if both\n  records individually pass verification.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-catch-record`** -- catch-quantity/species/trip-log data\n   logging only (crew id, vessel id, species, quantity, entry text).\n   Not a decision of any kind, and subject to the same scope-exclusion\n   free-text check as every other op.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- watch/duty scheduling logistics\n   only. Cannot carry a fishing-operation-execution/voyage-go-no-go\n   plan without tripping the scope-exclusion check if its free text\n   names a finalization/execution action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces an equipment-defect/\n   weather-hazard/crew-fatigue concern to a human; ALWAYS escalates\n   (governor's `always-escalate-ops`, unconditionally, at every\n   confidence level), NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY\n   channel through which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it\n   explicitly never resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself --\n   the human crew and vessel captain review and act entirely on their\n   own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- vessel/equipment supplies (ice,\n   bait, safety gear, net-repair supplies) procurement proposal,\n   gated by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000 always\n   escalates) like any office/facility procurement workflow. Not an\n   operational decision of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics\n   action.\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase,\nresembles directly finalizing a fishing-operation-execution decision,\ndeciding a voyage go/no-go in adverse conditions, or overriding a\nvessel captain's judgment -- these are structurally absent, confirmed\nby: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`deepfishery.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) a concretely-named\nforbidden-op fixture rejected at the governor-unit level\n(`deepfishery.governor-test/hard-on-op-not-in-allowlist`), and (c) a\ncontent-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op` field\n(`deepfishery.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases`,\n`deepfishery.governor/scope-violation?`), tested directly against\nfishing-operation-finalization, voyage-go/no-go and\ncaptain-override phrasings\n(`deepfishery.governor-test/hard-on-scope-exclusion-fishing-operation-finalization-phrase`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-exclusion-voyage-go-no-go-phrase`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-exclusion-captain-override-phrase`).\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 20, :assertions 45, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Deep-sea Fishery Crew Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:actor/governor "DeepSeaFisheryGovernor"), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :crew-member-verification :vessel-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-order-cost-threshold-escalation :safety-concern-always-escalates)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-6223"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6223"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6223)), (:actor/confidence-floor 0.6), (:test/simulator :deepfishery.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-6223 — Deep-sea Fishery Workers Vessel/Crew Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000 2607152500)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-6223)))